        <mxCell id="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-102" parent="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-97" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;rotatable=0;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" value="get(int index): Object" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28" width="440" y="138" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-135" parent="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-97" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;rotatable=0;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" value="indexOf(Object value): int" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28" width="440" y="166" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-99" parent="1" style="html=1;shadow=0;dashed=0;shape=mxgraph.bootstrap.rrect;rSize=5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#6C767D;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;spacing=10;" value="A dictionary stores elements, mainly for deduplication. Technically a dictionary is a JBON list of arbitrary primitives and/or DataObject&#39;s, that can be referred by their index. Opening a dictionary JBON automatically decodes it, and creates a caching layer to keep the values in memory." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="112" width="440" x="2450" y="2681" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-138" parent="1" style="html=1;shadow=0;dashed=0;shape=mxgraph.bootstrap.rrect;rSize=5;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;spacing=10;" value="The Lib-Data implements classes to handle structured data of the following types:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boolean,&amp;nbsp;Double,&amp;nbsp;Long&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(51, 51, 51), rgb(193, 193, 193));&quot;&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(51, 51, 51), rgb(193, 193, 193));&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(51, 51, 51), rgb(193, 193, 193));&quot;&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(51, 51, 51), rgb(193, 193, 193));&quot;&gt;Array, Map, Bytes or JTS Geometries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Whenever any other object is added into a map or array, an &lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;IllegalArgumentException&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; will be thrown. Actually, Byte, Short, and Integer are automatically converted into Long using a `Data.intern` call, so is a Float converted into Double. That is why there is no getter for Byte, Short, Integer or Float. They are simply never in a map or array.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="870" x="1450" y="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bNCgAfvZQ5hsA_kJCly6-142" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=26;fillColor=#dae8fc;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=1;marginBottom=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="Legend" vertex="1">
