        <mxCell id="XuQO3tHAvvKQnDVfzfl5-101" parent="1" style="html=1;shadow=0;dashed=0;shape=mxgraph.bootstrap.rrect;rSize=5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#6C767D;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;spacing=10;" value="Base class that can only be used inside `naksha.data`. All JSON objects have some features in common, for example they can be made immutable and proxies can detect changes done to the data object using the change-count. The sign-bit of the change-count is internally used to remember if the object is immutable." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="480" x="1240" y="399" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="XuQO3tHAvvKQnDVfzfl5-107" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=26;fillColor=#dae8fc;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=1;marginBottom=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;abstract&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;Proxy&amp;lt;O extends IObject, P extends Proxy&amp;lt;O,P&amp;gt;&amp;gt;" vertex="1">
