        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CrYzsB_NNo0B62X1mgjU-65" parent="CrYzsB_NNo0B62X1mgjU-51" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;rotatable=0;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" value="... more methods, especially added by extending classes" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28" width="680" y="306" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CrYzsB_NNo0B62X1mgjU-67" parent="1" style="html=1;shadow=0;dashed=0;shape=mxgraph.bootstrap.rrect;rSize=5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#6C767D;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;spacing=10;" value="Options are runtime enumerations. There are no enumerations in JSON, nor are there any in JBON. Actually, enumerations are not really needed, except from a programmers point of view. They are logical constraints. This is how the `Option` is implemented. When an Option is added into a map or array, not the option object is added, but the value it represents. A value can be turned into an Option instance using the static `get` method or using the `asOption` method in the `IObject`. Note that the given class must be a subclass of Option, not Option.class itself.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;W&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(108, 118, 125), rgb(131, 139, 145));&quot;&gt;hile it is possible to have multiple sub-classes of an option, there is one thing to remember: When creating a sub-class, the namespace class (the class directly extending Option), must invoke the `register(getClass())` from within its&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(108, 118, 125), rgb(131, 139, 145));&quot;&gt;constructor for each sub-class. This is important to get the class initialized and the statics registered with the enumeration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="680" x="1801" y="1020" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CrYzsB_NNo0B62X1mgjU-138" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=26;fillColor=#dae8fc;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=1;marginBottom=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;interface&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;TupleStorage &lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;implements&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Comparable&amp;lt;TupleStorage&amp;gt;" vertex="1">
